  {
   "text": "{\"explanations\":[{\"signal_id\":\"77cbf396-ae56-4750-9ace-a6d6283d3e08\",\"explanation\":\"At current burn, Datamarrow's cash covers about {{fact:3d20f048-c166-46e0-8861-1d90c619ef38}} months of operations, short enough that its ability to keep paying depends on new funding or cost cuts arriving soon. The falling runway covenant headroom and the cash covenant now below its minimum point the same way.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"ac0071f2-5d34-452b-aa18-5c5bcd7948cb\",\"explanation\":\"Negative headroom means unrestricted cash of {{fact:dd933902-67d2-4a16-b45e-74e0de748a96}} is below the covenant minimum of {{fact:f333b89d-4d27-489d-9610-89b687ea4fc0}}, so on these figures the covenant appears breached at October 31, not merely tight. Together with the short runway, this shows the cash cushion has run out ahead of the borrower's funding needs.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"8e42a5f8-6832-4227-aa6d-02a16c65e49d\",\"explanation\":\"Cash covenant headroom slid from {{fact:197c121f-7e91-4273-8a36-453a5d8d1ab1}} in August to {{fact:59d498c9-d219-4568-8398-293abf56dfef}} in September and {{fact:9776bf85-4868-48f0-b981-81214cd2b2f1}} in October. The steady decline shows the breach is the result of continued burn rather than a one-off dip, which makes a quick recovery less likely without new cash.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"766043e5-e4fd-4056-abab-295acd298f29\",\"explanation\":\"Runway covenant headroom fell from {{fact:4d5024dc-4ffa-4e10-bdfd-749c69fab4ae}} in August to {{fact:6874f8b3-ca06-4b29-a80f-4e460ca0fe3f}} in September and {{fact:43d454bb-6fa1-4042-b1a2-57b541bb9a7e}} in October, with runway of {{fact:f3ab609d-f31c-4a88-997b-8c1d36d40060}} months against a minimum of {{fact:4a0dd73f-970c-49a0-a66a-b603ca978dee}}. The covenant still passes, but if the pace continues it could follow the cash covenant below its minimum.\"}],\"ranking\":[\"77cbf396-ae56-4750-9ace-a6d6283d3e08\",\"ac0071f2-5d34-452b-aa18-5c5bcd7948cb\",\"8e42a5f8-6832-4227-aa6d-02a16c65e49d\",\"766043e5-e4fd-4056-abab-295acd298f29\"]}",
